// Merged into ~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc by install.sh under `agent.ocd-delegate`.
//
// There is deliberately no `model` key here. This file used to pin one, and
// that pinned id was delisted by the provider — leaving the installed agent
// permanently pointed at a model that no longer existed. ocd resolves a model
// at runtime and passes it explicitly on every dispatch (`--model`, see
// src/dispatch.ts), and refuses to dispatch at all without one rather than
// letting opencode fall back to its own default, which is very likely PAID.
// An agent-level model would therefore never be used, only rot. Keep it out;
// test/models.test.ts fails the build if a concrete model id reappears here.
//
// Permission key forms are NOT uniform, confirmed against opencode
// v1.18.16's own config validator and re-verified on v1.18.29 (not guessed):
//   - `bash`/`edit`/`read`/`external_directory`/`plan_enter`/`plan_exit`
//     accept the pattern-map form ({"*": "deny", "some-pattern*": "allow"}).
//   - `webfetch`/`doom_loop`/`question` REJECT pattern-map outright — using
//     it here broke config loading entirely (opencode errored with
//     "Expected PermissionActionConfig | undefined, got {"*":"deny"}"),
//     which in turn broke every other agent, including the pre-existing
//     `delegate` one, since an invalid config fails the whole file. Those
//     three keys only accept the bare-string form.
// (An earlier pass at this file suspected a second, separate issue — bare
// strings for `external_directory`/`doom_loop` silently resolving to "ask"
// instead of the declared "deny" on the pre-existing `delegate` agent.
// Re-checked directly against `opencode debug agent delegate`'s full
// resolved permission list: that agent's config also produces multiple
// entries per (permission, pattern) — base defaults, then this agent's own
// overrides — and the LAST entry for `doom_loop`/`external_directory` was
// already "deny", i.e. the override does apply. That first read only
// caught an early, non-winning entry in the array. `ocd doctor`'s
// agent_permissions check was already written to take the last matching
// entry, so no code changed here — only this comment, correcting the
// record.)
{
  "ocd-delegate": {
    "mode": "primary",
    "maxSteps": 40,
    "permission": {
      "edit": { "*": "allow" },
      "read": {
        "*": "allow",
        "*.env": "ask",
        "*.env.*": "ask",
        "*.env.example": "allow"
      },
      "bash": {
        "*": "allow",
        "git push*": "deny",
        "git push --force*": "deny",
        "git reset --hard*": "deny",
        "rm -rf*": "deny",
        "sudo*": "deny",
        "npm publish*": "deny",
        "npm unpublish*": "deny",
        "yarn publish*": "deny",
        "pnpm publish*": "deny"
      },
      "webfetch": "deny",
      "external_directory": { "*": "deny" },
      "doom_loop": "deny",
      "question": "deny",
      "plan_enter": { "*": "deny" },
      "plan_exit": { "*": "deny" }
    }
  }
}
